\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\b\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 Chairman
\u8217\'92s Report\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\b\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 Firstly
 I wish you and yours a very Happy and Peaceful New Year. \par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 The Paris
 Branch looks forward to a busy year, not least in celebrating its 90{\super th}
 Anniversary, since we were formed in May 1921, a month before the formation of 
the British Legion in the UK.  Your Committee is currently preparing to hold an 
Anniversary Dinner Dance in May. \par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 May I 
on your behalf thank the outgoing Committee on their work in the last Legion Year
.  By definition our work is voluntary and the Paris Branch has relied  heavily 
on our hard-working Secretary, Janet Warby,  and Treasurer, David Blanchard,  to
 keep the show on the road. As you know David Blanchard stood down at the AGM after
 20 years in post.  At the time of writing we have not yet found a successor, so
 that David is prepared to act as Acting Treasurer until we find the right candidate
.  If  you have friends who would rise to this challenge I should be very pleased
 to hear from you.\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 Next on
 your behalf I wish to thank our Poppy Organizer Joyce Gilhooley. Final figures 
are still being computed, but she believes her result in the 2010 Appeal is close
 to last year\u8217\'92s record total.  To achieve this during an economic downturn
 speaks for itself, and we congratulate her warmly. \par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 Because
 of the inclement weather on the date of our Christmas Tombola we were obliged to
 postpone the draw to January 20{\super th}. The prize-winners are listed below 
on Pages 3-4.  We thank warmly all those who participated.\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 Alongside
 our Welfare and Social activities we are constantly reminded of our Remembrance
 duties.  We plan a visit to the battlefields of the Somme once more in the Spring
.  As usual our guide will be Branch member Colonel Oliver Warman, late Welsh Guards
. We will release details shortly so that you can put the dates in your diary.\par
}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28 A little
 nearer home it is high time that we held a ceremony on one of  the sites of  Commonwealth
 war graves in the Paris area;.  High on that list is Les Gonards in Versailles.  
Again details will be released in good time. \par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qj\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs24\kerning28\tab\tab
\tab{\f1\tab{\b\fs32\~We will remember them\~\par}}}

